          "en": "| Type | Example | Remark |\n|---|---|---|\n| `string` | `\"eu-west-3\"` | Always in **double** quotes |\n| `number` | `50`, `0.5` | Integer or decimal, no quotes |\n| `bool` | `true`, `false` | Lowercase, no quotes |\n| `list` | `[\"a\", \"b\"]` | Ordered, indexed from 0 |\n| `map` | `{ Team = \"ops\" }` | Keys and values of the same type |\n| `object` | `{ port = 5432, tls = true }` | Attributes of different types |\n| `null` | `null` | \"No value\": the argument is ignored |\n\nInside a string, `${ ... }` inserts a value: `\"/${local.project}/app\"` (interpolation).\nFor multi-line text, use a *heredoc*: `<<-EOT` ... `EOT`.\n\nThree comment styles exist: `#` (the recommended one), `//` and `/* ... */` for several lines.\nFinally, all `.tf` files in the same directory are read **together**: the order of blocks and the\nsplit into files (`main.tf`, `variables.tf`, `outputs.tf`) is a readability convention, not a\nlanguage constraint.\n"
